{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Water shall flow, etc.</b> The intent, according to their words (Shemot Rabbah 28:6), is that every individual of Israel received a portion in the Torah from Sinai, and to this alludes ״מוֹרָשָׁה״, and they expounded (Pesachim 49b): do not read מוֹרָשָׁה (inheritance) but מְאוֹרָשָׂה (betrothed). And he says here that whatever innovations one produces in the Torah are ״from his bucket״ — from what Moses drew, for everything is alluded to in the written Torah." "<b>And he says</b> the expression <b>bucket</b> to say that in relation to the great gate (Binah) that HaShem is destined to reveal to Israel at the end of generations in the days of King Mashiach, which is the fiftieth gate of Binah — all forty-nine are in the category of a bucket by comparison. And he says that although now it is a bucket, the seed of Israel will merit to draw abundant waters, which is the fiftieth gate, and this is his saying <b>and his seed in abundant waters</b>:" "<b>And higher than Agag shall be his king.</b> Here he revealed the everlasting kingdom of Israel, which began from Agag, that is, the kingdom of Amalek — the first act that Saul performed, and from there the kingdom of Saul was cut off and given to his good friend, who is David. And the reason he called the beginning of his kingdom ״from Agag״ is to point to the cause of the matter that came about through Agag — meaning that Saul left him alive and did not kill him, as they said, of blessed memory (Megillah 13a), that on that night Agag spawned the seed of Amalek, and this was the cause for the uprooting of Saul's kingdom and for the exalting of the kingdom of the House of David. <b>And his kingdom shall be exalted</b> — this is the kingdom of Mashiach, who is David, as it is written (Ezekiel 37:24) ״וְעַבְדִּי דָוִד מֶלֶךְ עֲלֵיהֶם״; he shall be high and lifted up exceedingly, as stated in Isaiah (Isaiah 52:13)." "<b>Further,</b> it intends in his saying <b>and higher than Agag</b>, that the beginning of the activity of King Mashiach is the war against Amalek, for all of Amalek descends from Agag as is known. And they said, of blessed memory (Tanchuma, end of parashat Tetze), that the Holy One, blessed be He, said: ״The throne is not complete until the seed of Amalek is obliterated״ — <b>and his kingdom shall be exalted</b> over all the world."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:48.464809821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}